      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I want to bring this post back and say that I love this idea as way to automatically tailor an avatar to a viewer's preferences without fully blocking it. This is also not entirely unprecedented since the default IsOnFriendsList parameter already allows avatars to use different settings for friends vs non friends. This would seem to be just more of the same.\n\nTo me a warning about this shouldn't be necessary since the whole point of the content gating system is to keep undesirable content hidden.\n\nThe upside I see to this is that I see it as a relatively easy implementation on VRChat's side (with my admittedly limited understanding). The downside it that it would require adoption by the community but I see this as one of the best options to at least start to make a user's content gating settings more useful.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
