  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Add additional local avatar parameters that can be used to partially gate content on avatars. This can be used to enable or disable parts of avatars without blocking the whole / entirety of the avatar. Good examples would be making an avatars appearance only capable of the “suggestive”, “adult language”, or “gore” categories if both Animations are enabled and also the content is not gated. This might not be entirely necessary with the introduction of the Avatar Impostor system, however it would still be ideal to provide users with a way to gate the content. \n\nIf any of those parameters are used within the avatar, there should be a partial gating warning that will show that parts of the avatar have been blocked but not all of it, similar to the safety settings warnings. There should also be an option to add gating conditions to avatar parameters or Expression Menu options themselves, preventing users from accessing or seeing any options which are gated by that user’s settings. This will allow avatars to be accurate for both users. Anyone using the avatar will be unable to access content they have gated for themselves, and anyone viewing the avatar will be unable to see such content on the avatar at all, but in both cases both users will be able to interact with the avatar without any issues.\n\nEdit: This concept can also work for worlds via Udon variables. Good example would be enabling or disabling gore in a battle arena or horror game world, or censoring usage of adult language. Users should ideally also be able to see this as warnings / information. Any world or avatar whos content can be “censored” to adapt to user preferences should be allowed to do so, in the best interest of both things such as public avatars and worlds, so that all users may be able to experience and interact with them without issue *and* without violating their choices towards content they wish not to see.",
